The parity of $i^2$ is the same as $i$, hence
$$\sum_{i=m}^n (-1)^{i^2}x^{2i}=\sum_{i=m}^n (-1)^{i}x^{2i}$$
then use the general geometric sum we get
\begin{align*}
\sum_{i=m}^n (-1)^{i^2}x^{2i}&=\sum_{i=m}^n (-1)^{i}x^{2i}=\sum_{i=m}^n \left ( -x^{2} \right )^{i}\\&= \frac{\left ( -x^2 \right )^m - \left ( -x^2 \right )^{n+1}}{1 - \left ( -x^2 \right )}\\
&=\frac{\left ( -1 \right )^{m}x^{2m}+\left ( -1 \right )^{n}x^{2n+2}}{1+x^2}
\end{align*}

